1
00:00:00,635 --> 00:00:02,129
This is my ER bill.

2
00:00:02,179 --> 00:00:03,952
Twelve hundred and eighty-four dollars…

3
00:00:04,002 --> 00:00:05,451
for a sprained wrist.

4
00:00:07,635 --> 00:00:09,675
Forty-three percent of Americans have had

5
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:11,859
a medical bill they thought was wrong.

6
00:00:11,942 --> 00:00:14,144
Fewer than half ever push back.

7
00:00:14,194 --> 00:00:15,596
And the ones who do?

8
00:00:15,646 --> 00:00:17,525
More than a third get it cut.

9
00:00:21,835 --> 00:00:23,933
So why not just ask an AI?

10
00:00:23,983 --> 00:00:25,744
Because to ask, I'd have to hand over my

11
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:28,588
name, my birthday, my insurance ID…

12
00:00:28,638 --> 00:00:30,134
my diagnosis.

13
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,460
So we built Airlock.

14
00:00:39,112 --> 00:00:41,525
Airlock splits the work across a wall.

15
00:00:41,575 --> 00:00:43,872
On your laptop, Gemini Nano reads the

16
00:00:43,922 --> 00:00:46,805
bill, in only-on-device mode,

17
00:00:46,855 --> 00:00:48,832
so it can never quietly fall back to the

18
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:49,536
cloud.

19
00:00:49,586 --> 00:00:52,096
Your identity goes into a vault.

20
00:00:52,146 --> 00:00:54,772
Only anonymous line items cross,

21
00:00:54,822 --> 00:00:56,962
and cloud Gemini audits them against real

22
00:00:57,012 --> 00:01:00,382
billing rules, grounded in Google Search.

23
00:01:03,043 --> 00:01:03,729
Watch.

24
00:01:03,779 --> 00:01:05,953
Nano reads the photo, right here.

25
00:01:06,003 --> 00:01:08,213
Name, member ID, birthday,

26
00:01:08,263 --> 00:01:09,601
the hospital…

27
00:01:09,651 --> 00:01:11,693
each one becomes a token.

28
00:01:11,743 --> 00:01:14,020
The real values stay in an encrypted

29
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:15,823
vault, on this laptop.

30
00:01:22,548 --> 00:01:24,270
And before a single byte leaves,

31
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:26,450
a guard, written in code,

32
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,150
not in a prompt, checks it.

33
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,260
Hide an ID in a description,

34
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:33,420
and the request is blocked.

35
00:01:40,635 --> 00:01:43,244
It found the X-ray, billed twice.

36
00:01:43,294 --> 00:01:44,857
Two hundred and twelve dollars.

37
00:01:44,907 --> 00:01:47,446
And it questioned a level-five ER code for

38
00:01:47,496 --> 00:01:49,745
a sprained wrist, and told me which rule

39
00:01:49,795 --> 00:01:51,105
it's relying on.

40
00:01:58,756 --> 00:02:00,558
The cloud drafts the dispute letter with

41
00:02:00,608 --> 00:02:02,208
placeholders.

42
00:02:02,258 --> 00:02:04,704
Back on the device, Airlock fills in the

43
00:02:04,754 --> 00:02:05,896
real details.

44
00:02:05,946 --> 00:02:07,867
The finished letter never leaves your

45
00:02:07,917 --> 00:02:08,926
laptop.

46
00:02:14,795 --> 00:02:16,697
Turn the internet off, and the private

47
00:02:16,747 --> 00:02:18,660
half still works.

48
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:21,113
Explanations run on-device when they can,

49
00:02:21,163 --> 00:02:23,688
and in the cloud when they can't,

50
00:02:23,738 --> 00:02:25,943
because they carry no identity.

51
00:02:30,890 --> 00:02:31,710
One SDK.

52
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:34,460
Three inference modes, each one chosen on

53
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:35,510
purpose.

54
00:02:39,435 --> 00:02:39,849
Airlock.

55
00:02:39,899 --> 00:02:40,604
Fight the bill…

56
00:02:40,654 --> 00:02:41,918
not your privacy.
